   $q$On which interval is $f(x) = -x^2 + 6x - 5$ increasing?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x < -3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-in-h"},{"text":"$x > 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-intervals-for-downward-parabola"},{"text":"$x < 3$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$1 < x < 5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-interval-between-zeros"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x < 3$$q$, $q$The vertex is at $x = -\frac{6}{2(-1)} = 3$, and $a = -1$ means the parabola opens downward. It rises until the vertex, so it is increasing for $x < 3$. The choice $1 < x < 5$ is where the graph is above the x-axis (the zeros are $1$ and $5$), which is a different question.$q$, 'draft', null)
