  ('b9323939-ae6f-5926-9620-3230b7bc672b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'quadratic-functions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$What is the range of the function $y = 3x^2 + 12x + 7$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$y \\ge -5$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$y \\ge -2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-x-coordinate-for-range"},{"text":"$y \\ge 7$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-c-as-minimum"},{"text":"$y \\le -5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-inequality-for-upward-parabola"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$y \ge -5$$q$, $q$The vertex is at $x = -\frac{12}{2 \cdot 3} = -2$, and $y = 3(4) + 12(-2) + 7 = 12 - 24 + 7 = -5$. Since $a = 3$ is positive, the parabola opens upward, so $-5$ is the lowest output and the range is $y \ge -5$. The choice $y \ge 7$ uses the y-intercept, which is not the lowest point.$q$, 'draft', null)
